series 10 (1060, 1070, 1080) series and can test this out I would appreciate it if you could confirm if this happens. (You can use the MRP and see if the building has that black artifact)\n\n**Edit:** tested on the 5060 and indeed the artifacts do not happen there. Only in the 1070. It could be either a driver thing or the model, but more people with the series 10 would need to test the MRP to check up on that. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5525906674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5548929762","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122984#issuecomment-5548929762","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122984","id":5548929762,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSr3y4g","user":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-05T03:05:10Z","updated_at":"2026-09-05T03:05:10Z","body":"I found a couple more things that \"fixes\" the artifacts.\n\nTurning on the Material's **Refraction/Grow or Proximity fade**.\n\nWhich is really strange. Looking at the grow code for example, the only thing it seems to do it add \n\"VERTEX += NORMAL * grow;\"\nBut even with grow = 0 it fixes these artifacts.\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/34d06658a85845111a50db9e485ec4a0701d4298/scene/resources/material.cpp#L1440-L1444\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3a76c701-ca23-4fb4-ba33-fb17be4f3208\n\n---\nI also tried random things like exporting the models with tangent data, messing with any and all import options within Godot and changing configurations of the NVIDEA drivers but nothing else seems to help.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5548929762/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5734889840","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122984#issuecomment-5734889840","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122984","id":5734889840,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVdN5cA","user":{"login":"Yni-Viar","id":81305791,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMzA1Nzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81305791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yni-Viar","html_url":"https://github.com/Yni-Viar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yni-Viar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yni-Viar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yni-Viar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yni-Viar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yni-Viar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yni-Viar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yni-Viar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yni-Viar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yni-Viar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-18T19:07:04Z","updated_at":"2026-09-18T19:13:00Z","body":"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a913184-4bf1-41a9-a0e6-9ee261d5d1d8\n\nCould not reproduce.\nGodot v4.8.dev6 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor (1920x1080 @ 74.97 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8266) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-10400F CPU @ 2.90GHz (12 threads) - 15.89 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\nI think, it may be old NVIDIA driver bug, that was already fixed.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5734889840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5744221430","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122984#issuecomment-5744221430","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122984","id":5744221430,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVmHc9g","user":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-19T18:09:44Z","updated_at":"2026-09-19T18:09:44Z","body":"> -30000.mp4 \n> Could not reproduce. Godot v4.8.dev6 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor (1920x1080 @ 74.97 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8266) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-10400F CPU @ 2.90GHz (12 threads) - 15.89 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n> \n> I think, it may be old NVIDIA driver bug, that was already fixed.\n\n**You are probably right.** \nI also had a very strange and bad shadow artifact issue happen on the new Wanderburg game that is made with Unity.\nWhere the shadows seems to get stuck and dragged along while moving.\n\n<img width=\"335\" height=\"154\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/04b7a957-349e-4445-a296-081ba41a8117\" />\n\nIt is probably some undefined behavior on the driver then.\n\nSadly I can't update my driver. I tried a few times and had to revert.\nI think the new driver depends on something from a newer version of windows to work properly. \nGiving me constant BSOD and rebooting the PC, making it unusable.\nAnd I'm stuck on windows 1803 due to not having enough space to upgrade anymore in my 100 GB OS drive.\n\n----\n\nI'll close this issue then.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5744221430/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]